  "completed": [
    "Only an exact frozen topology object that has reached controller, broker, worker or guardian-watch final state may transfer an endpoint, and only an endpoint assigned to that final role may be selected.",
    "The topology lock, process/thread owner, absolute deadline and socket identity are revalidated immediately before mutation.",
    "The endpoint is removed from the topology before the one detach attempt, so the topology can never close it after ownership transfer and cannot retry an ambiguous detach.",
    "A detach failure retains the socket object. A post-detach identity failure retains the raw descriptor and recorded identity. Neither ambiguity is closed as a possible replacement descriptor.",
    "A successful detach produces one private authority object with an exact descriptor identity and process/thread owner. Its snapshot contains no descriptor, socket identity or endpoint name.",
    "The authority can either transfer the descriptor once or close it once. Transfer validates identity before removing prior ownership; close removes ownership and consumes the close attempt before the final identity check.",
    "A changed descriptor is never returned or closed. Failed, transferred or close-attempted authorities cannot be reused or retried.",
    "All endpoints assigned to every final role were exercised through the synthetic transfer path without changing the frozen v0.115 topology source or any prior evidence."
  ],
  "fixed_transfer": {
    "accepted_topology_stages": [
      "broker",
      "controller",
      "guardian_watch",
      "worker"
    ],
    "detach_attempts_per_endpoint": 1,
    "authority_dispositions": [
